sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  box rgba(234, 88, 12, 0.10) Your agent
    participant S as Claude Code or Codex session
  end
  box rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.10) loadout
    participant H as hook-session-start
    participant M as maintenance
  end
  box rgba(22, 163, 74, 0.10) Your machine
    participant G as Kit and personal repos
    participant C as ~/.claude, ~/.claude.json
    participant X as ~/.codex
  end

  S->>H: session starts
  H-->>S: queued notices
  opt daily pull or weekly check due
    H-)M: start detached
    Note over S,H: the session does not wait
    activate M
    Note over M: one run at a time
    opt daily, unless LOADOUT_NO_AUTO_PULL=1
      M->>G: git pull --ff-only
      Note over G: git refuses on its own when a local<br/>change would be overwritten, and<br/>a notice names the files
      G-->>M: new commits, none, or a refusal
      opt new commits arrived
        opt Claude Code on
          M->>C: merge settings, add personal MCP
          M->>C: relink skills and hook scripts
        end
        opt Codex on and usable
          M->>X: refresh rules, config, hooks and skills
          Note over X: plugins with the Codex CLI or the extension's own codex
        end
      end
    end
    opt weekly
      M->>M: check tool versions
      Note right of M: notice only,<br/>never installs
    end
    M--)H: queue notices for the next session
    deactivate M
  end
